From: packetloss404 <packetloss404@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:44:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 02/10] tools: refuse dotenv secret files in read_file,
 search_codebase, and @-mentions

packetcode reads provider API keys from <project>/.env and
~/.packetcode/.env and never injects them into subprocess environments,
but the model-facing read tools had no matching rule. read_file is a
read-only tool no built-in profile prompts for, so the model could inline
the same file into a transcript that is sent to the provider, persisted
under ~/.packetcode/sessions, and visible to every later tool call. A
project command file (repository content) could do the same through an
@-mention.

One name rule, tools.IsSecretFilePath, now covers read_file (supplied and
resolved path), all three search_codebase engines, and @-mention
expansion: `.env` and `.env.*` are refused; `.env.example`, `.env.sample`,
`.env.template` and `.env.dist` are not. ripgrep search over-excludes
`.env.example` because a later positive glob would otherwise re-include the
file. execute_command is untouched: it is approval-gated and the command
is shown to the user.

Audit patch P02. Rollback: git revert this commit; behaviour change only,
no on-disk format changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
